From c7896253e3846760b57f3f53b42139dc91d71a6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:58:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban_kept_reader: one process-wide pool, at most 2
 kept connections per board file

`kanban_kept_reader` kept one SQLite connection per (thread, board file) for the life of the thread. Its only
caller, `kanban_decompose.list_triage_ids`, runs from the gateway dispatcher's auto-decompose tick on the
`hermes-gateway-default` executor, whose threads never exit, so every executor thread ended up holding a
connection to every board: mac-mini-1 gateway pid 85886 (core 3059f72ea6) had 12 executor threads x 4 boards,
and 48 idle connections measured offline cost 42.4 MB (t_01a1cf67a93c05b6, t_01a1db28414ae096).

Kept connections now live in one process-wide pool keyed by the resolved board path:

- `MAX_PER_BOARD = 2` kept per board, `MAX_KEPT = 32` in total (past it the least recently borrowed idle entry is
  closed; when every other entry is borrowed the new one is not kept and closes on its borrow's exit).
  `MAX_PER_THREAD` is gone.
- `reading()` takes an idle entry of the board with a non-blocking `lock.acquire`, opens one while the board has
  fewer than `MAX_PER_BOARD` (an in-flight open holds its slot via `_opening`), and otherwise yields an ordinary
  per-call connection (closed on exit, `stats["fallbacks"]` += 1). It never waits for a kept connection.
- Unchanged: `_still_live` before every borrow and reopen on failure, `query_only`, `check_same_thread=False`, the
  `_evict` generation hook, `close_all()`, `release_gone()`, the fenced and read-only-schema fallbacks, dropping a
  connection left in a transaction or whose body raised `sqlite3.Error`, the `stats` keys.
- Thread-exit handling (`_tls`, `_ThreadEntries`, `_orphans`, `_drain_orphans`) is deleted. `_registry` is now the
  pool itself (an OrderedDict in borrow order); `_registry_lock` still guards map operations only.
- `list_triage_ids` and the dispatcher are unchanged. `kanban_gone_board_handles` only calls `release_gone()`
  (it never read `MAX_PER_THREAD`); its docstring now says "pooled".

