Rewritten tests in `tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_kept_reader.py` (per-thread ownership -> pool):

- `test_cap_eviction_skips_a_borrowed_entry_and_closes_the_idle_one`: old: `MAX_PER_THREAD` other boards opened
  inside a borrow of A leave A in this thread's map (`_mine()`), the oldest idle closed, map size
  `MAX_PER_THREAD`. New: same shape against `MAX_KEPT` (monkeypatched to 4): A stays in the pool, the least
  recently borrowed idle entry is closed, pool size `MAX_KEPT`, `close_all() == MAX_KEPT`.
- `test_cap_overflow_with_every_entry_borrowed_closes_the_evicted_one_on_exit`: old: with every entry borrowed the
  OLDEST (A) was detached from the thread map and closed on its exit. New: the NEWEST is not kept (A stays), every
  borrowed connection still works, the newest is closed on exit, A stays open, pool size `MAX_KEPT`.
- `test_exited_thread_connections_are_closed_by_the_next_borrow` ->
  `test_exited_thread_connections_stay_in_the_pool_and_close_all_closes_them`: old: an exited thread's
  connection is closed by the next borrow on another thread. New: it is served to the next borrower
  (`conn is got["conn"]`) and `close_all()` closes it (returns 1).
- Helper `_thread_map()` (`kept._mine()`) -> `_kept_keys()` (open entries in `kept._registry`).

Added (mutation killers): `test_a_failed_kept_open_releases_its_board_slot`,
`test_an_unkeepable_open_releases_its_board_slot`, `test_an_open_in_flight_counts_toward_max_per_board`.
Mutants (each condition flipped/dropped, all three files run): drop either `_unreserve`, drop the `_opening` term,
`if held >= MAX_PER_BOARD` -> `if False`, drop `move_to_end`, drop the detached `keep = False`, drop the cap's
`_registry.pop(new)`: all 7 killed.
